      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.mark.bohairic_ed:15",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉⲣⲉⲛⲉϥϩⲙϩⲁⲗ ⲟⲗⲙ ⲉϩⲟⲩⲛ ⲉⲣⲟϥ · ⲁⲩⲱ ϣⲁⲣⲉⲛⲉϥⲟⲩⲣⲏⲏⲧⲉ ⲙⲛⲛⲉϥⲙⲉⲗⲟⲥ **ⲡⲱϩ** ⲛⲥⲉⲧⲁⲩⲟ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ⲛϩⲉⲛⲁⲕⲁⲑⲁⲣⲥⲓⲁ ⲉⲩⲟϣ ·",
      "english": "and his servant would be obliged to carry him to his house; and his feet and his (other) members would burst from time to time, and eject large quantities of unclean matter.",
      "source": "Encomium on Victor part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pscelestinus.encomium.budge:1-31",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲥⲁⲧⲟⲧϥ ⲉϥⲛⲏⲟⲩ ⲉⲡϣⲱⲓ ⲉⲃⲟⲗ ϧⲉⲛⲡⲓⲙⲱⲟⲩ ⲁϥⲛⲁⲩ ⲉⲛⲓⲫⲏⲟⲩⲓ ⲉⲁⲩ**ⲫⲱϧ** ⲟⲩⲟϩ ⲡⲓⲡⲛⲉⲩⲙⲁ ⲁϥⲓ ⲉϧⲣⲏⲓ ⲉϫⲱϥ ⲙⲫⲣⲏϯ ⲛⲟⲩϭⲣⲟⲙⲡⲓ",
      "english": "Immediately coming up from the water, he saw the heavens parting, and the Spirit descending on him like a dove.",
      "source": "Bohairic Gospel of Mark 1 (Digital Edition)",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.mark.bohairic_ed:1",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲙⲉⲣⲉⲗⲁⲁⲩ ⲛⲉϫⲧⲟⲉⲓⲥ ⲛϣⲁⲉⲓ ⲉⲣⲛϣⲧⲏⲛ ⲙⲡⲗϭⲉ ⲉϣⲱⲡⲉ ⲙⲙⲟⲛ ⲧⲧⲟⲉⲓⲥ ⲛϣⲁⲓ ⲛⲁϥⲓⲡⲕⲱⲧⲉ ⲙⲙⲁⲩ ⲛⲧⲉϣⲧⲏⲛ ⲙⲡⲗϭⲉ ⲛⲥ**ⲡⲱϩ** ⲛϩⲟⲩⲟ .",
      "english": "No one sews a piece of unshrunk cloth on an old garment, or else the patch shrinks and the new tears away from the old, and a worse hole is made.",
      "source": "41_Mark_2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.mark.sahidica:2",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
